# Hangfire and scripts

- The poll job is `ScriptPollJob`. Hangfire automatic retry stays off. Folder numbering owns the 4 attempts.
- `[DisableConcurrentExecution]` stays on the job so two polls cannot apply the same script.
- Register the recurring job on startup. In-memory storage is expected to be empty after a restart.
- DDL, DML, and data go through DbUp in one transaction per script, with `CommandTimeoutSeconds`.
- Query scripts are not journaled.
- Journal schema and table stay on the target database. Do not point Hangfire storage at that database.
- Script kind is the inbox subfolder (`ddl`, `dml`, `data`, `query`) or a first line `-- kind: ...`.
- Run order is ddl, then dml, then data, then query, then file name.
- Missing-column repair may add a nullable column only. Record the diagnostic text next to the attempt.
